  "closure_unit": {
    "outcome": "Define the typed GPU client contract every Studio module uses toward the one Handshake GPU owner: grant handle, admission request (operation, module, client, device), budget and retained-memory accounting fields, settle-once release, device-loss rebind, typed Unavailable/Lost outcomes. Bind hsk-studio-render-gpu to that contract (its own GpuContext::acquire instance and BackendChoice leave the product path) and ship a transient in-process adapter so asset-local proof can run before the owner exists. Vulkan is the only product backend; the adapter's result is evidence, never host acceptance. The real owner, issuer and registered capability are WP-KERNEL-012 MT-203 work and are consumed here, never re-implemented.",
    "requirement_refs": [
      ".GOV/docs_repo/wp-studio-module-work/research/integration-refactor-inventory-20261030.json#/refactor_items"
    ],
    "acceptance_refs": [
      "MT-36248/AC-HOST-001",
      "MT-36248/AC-HOST-002",
      "MT-36248/AC-HOST-003",
      "MT-36248/AC-HOST-004",
      "MT-36248/AC-HOST-005",
      "MT-36248/AC-HOST-006"
    ],
    "materialized_acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "MT-36248/AC-HOST-001",
        "text": "The client contract is a typed port with no wgpu, ash or Vulkan type in any public signature; every GPU operation of render-gpu, composite's GPU path and the display path requests admission through it and settles exactly once (HBR-HOST-003)."
      },
      {
        "id": "MT-36248/AC-HOST-002",
        "text": "Attribution of module, client and device is carried on every allocation and retained buffer; budget and retained-memory numbers are measured, not estimated, and estimates are kept apart where they exist (GUI-DESKTOP-029/030)."
      },
      {
        "id": "MT-36248/AC-HOST-003",
        "text": "Cancellation, logout and pane close never release in-flight ownership before settlement; a late release or a double release is a typed error with a test (GUI-DESKTOP-033..036)."
      },
      {
        "id": "MT-36248/AC-HOST-004",
        "text": "Device unavailable and device lost are typed outcomes with rebind through the owner; no silent CPU fallback and no skipped-as-PASS test (GUI-DESKTOP-037/038, HBR-HOST-003)."
      },
      {
        "id": "MT-36248/AC-HOST-005",
        "text": "The transient in-process adapter is marked asset-local in its DESCRIPTOR, uses Vulkan first on Windows, and is excluded from host acceptance; the first adoption of the real owner (MT-203) replaces it without changing any module's public contract."
      },
      {
        "id": "MT-36248/AC-HOST-006",
        "text": "Dependency pins hold at wgpu 27.0.1 / egui 0.33.3 until Kumihimo's pinned revision is verified (Operator decision D2)."
      }
    ],
    "spec_basis_refs": [
      ".GOV/spec/master-spec-v02.225/spec-modules/15-native-desktop-gui-vulkan-gpu-ownership.md#GUI-DESKTOP-025",
      ".GOV/spec/master-spec-v02.225/spec-modules/15-native-desktop-gui-vulkan-gpu-ownership.md#GUI-DESKTOP-028",
